From 2bc0f6975708f4221c24123207c5660d49c27cb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:46:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Network] Projector control: the player controls and
 subtitles inside a scope picture

An owner of a JVC NZ800 said that the player controls cannot be seen
with a scope film, in the anamorphic mode and with a lens memory that
zooms and blanks: the projector zooms or stretches the 16:9 frame
beyond a 2.35:1 to 2.40:1 screen above and below it, and Estuary draws
its controls, its clock, the seek bar and the notices at the top and
bottom of the frame, where the screen is not.

While a video plays and the projector shows a scope picture (the
control has taken the lens memory or the anamorphic mode A to D of the
wide or widest pictures: ShowsScope()), they are now kept in a band of
the shape of the picture, 2.40:1 at least, the narrowest scope screen
(SafeBand(), ProjectorPolicy.h). A new setting, "Player controls inside
a scope picture", has "While the projector shows a scope picture" (the
default: without the projector control nothing changes), "Always while
a video plays" (for a projector zoomed or set for scope by hand; the
thread of the control then runs with no projector, to know whether a
video plays) and Off.

The skin: the control posts the inset to the Home window on the thread
of the interface (the builtins SetProperty and ClearProperty, as Kodi's
own code posts them), as hades.osd.inset (in units of 1080) and as
hades.osd.insetsteps, its steps of 4 to 128 ("_4_8_128_" for 140, a band
of 2.40:1 in 16:9). Estuary's controls at the bottom (VideoOSD.xml,
DialogSeekBar.xml) slide up by it, those at the top (the top bar of
Custom_1109_TopBarOverlay.xml, DialogNotification.xml,
DialogVolumeBar.xml, the back button of the touch mode) slide down: a
conditional slide for each step (HadesOsdInsetUp and HadesOsdInsetDown,
Includes_Animations.xml), as Kodi adds up the slides of a control. A
skin loaded again loses the properties of its windows: they are posted
again every 10 s while there is a band. The player information page,
taller than the band, is left as it is.

The subtitles: CRenderManager narrows the view of the overlays to the
same band (SubtitleBand()), for a fullscreen video in 2D, and keeps the
bitmap subtitles inside it as it keeps them on the screen while the
picture is zoomed to its active area. Text subtitles are then placed at
the bottom of the band ("Bottom of screen") or of the picture inside it
("Bottom of video"), at the size they have on a scope screen; subtitles
in the black bars find no room under the picture and stay in it.
